Z||000000||fierosound||01-30-2001||07:40 PM||||Just passing this on...<P>Hello Gang:<BR>I discovered a company (Sunstar America) that makes 1/18 scale American model cars. Their website is: <A HREF="http://www.sunstartoys.com" TARGET=_blank>www.sunstartoys.com</A>   The company has an email address as well : uscic@aol.com<P>The  president or CEO of the company's name is Sherman.  My recent email to him regarding making a model of our beloved Fiero, got the response that: "we thought about making the GT late models but changed out minds. I do not know for sure the demand for them."<P>If everybody on our list emailed him like I have done and requested a model, we may get one as they make a model of the's "Corvair" and I am sure that there are many, many more Fiero owners that want a diecast model of their car.<P>So everybody, please bombard them with emails requesting they immediately consider making a 1/18 scale diecast model of the Fiero.<P>Thanks,<BR>L.W.||||reg||14
Z||000001||hugh||01-30-2001||08:11 PM||||Done!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||01-30-2001||10:17 PM||||I wrote them this letter:<P>Subj:	Fiero Die Cast models<BR>Date:	1/30/01 10:03:18 PM Eastern Standard Time<BR>From:	Dalelee22<BR>To:	USCIC@aol.com<P>Have you ever considered making a 1/24 or 1/18 scale die cast model of the Late, Great, Pontiac Fiero. I own three of these fine automobiles and I'm sure that the response you would recieve would be fabulous !!! I would prefer a rendition of the 87-88 Formula/coupe body style. Primarily because even the plastic model companys did not produce this body style. <P>This is a link to just one of very many online Fiero clubs on the net...Post something here about the possibility of a Fiero die cast and check the response.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.pennock.nl/forum.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pennock.nl/forum.htm</A> <P>We are at near 2000 members and growing !!!!!!!!                  Thanks, Dale<P>Sorry guys I had to plug for my favorite body style...lol<P>||||reg||1
